  "title": "Correct token and USD accounting for Codex usage: cached input is part of input_tokens, and cache reads are priced as cache reads",
  "spec": "Why: usage analysis 2026-10-01: Pool._usage_tokens (pool.py around 311) sums input_tokens + cached_input_tokens + cache_read_input_tokens + cache creation + output. Codex usage reports input_tokens INCLUDING the cached part (cached_input_tokens is a subset), so cached tokens are counted twice and priced at the full rate via [limits].default_tokens_per_usd (250k/USD). Example: T-0237 counted 779k tokens vs 273k real; the scorecard shows sol $1,408 and astra $917, not comparable with Claude. Callers: bus.py:378-381 (run-row usd), executor.py:202, pool.py:257-262 (reservations), 308, 394-395 (accounting). Claude usage (input_tokens excludes cache reads/creation) is correct today and must stay unchanged.\nWhat: in _usage_tokens, when cached_input_tokens is present treat it as part of input_tokens (do not add it); keep the Claude keys as they are. In the derived-usd path, weight cached_input_tokens and cache_read_input_tokens by [limits].cache_read_weight (new key, default 0.1, documented in .orchestrator/pool.toml is NOT in scope: read it with a default in code). Recorded usd/total_cost_usd keep priority. Do not rewrite historical run rows; the fix applies to new rows and to on-the-fly derivations.\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1403. Commit first, then run the focused tests in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate. Acceptance ids are tests/<file>.py::<method name>; write tests as unittest.TestCase methods using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_pool.py::test_codex_usage_counts_cached_input_once passes: Pool._usage_tokens({'input_tokens': 1000, 'cached_input_tokens': 900, 'output_tokens': 50}) == 1050 and a Claude-shaped usage {'input_tokens': 100, 'cache_read_input_tokens': 900, 'cache_creation_input_tokens': 10, 'output_tokens': 50} still totals 1060",
    "tests/test_pool.py::test_derived_usd_weights_cache_reads passes: usd_of on usage without a recorded usd charges cached_input_tokens and cache_read_input_tokens at [limits].cache_read_weight (default 0.1) of the full rate and everything else at the full rate; a recorded usd or total_cost_usd still wins",
    "existing tests in tests/test_pool.py pass; .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
